(* The words of the admin pages in French: each text they show, as Say gives it, and those of the live screen and of
   Ceres (its band of keys, its page of no route, its errors of the screen) that reach them. An app's own words come
   after them (Run's words). tests/translated.test.ce walks the pages for each Say and checks it has its French here,
   with the names of its values. The English has its own forms where a text counts: 1 row, 2 rows. *)
use src/i18n

(** The catalogue of the admin pages, in French.

      i18n.Say(Words, "fr", "Sign out") --> "Se déconnecter"
      i18n.Say(Words, "fr", "{N} members", {N: 1}) --> "1 membre"
      i18n.Say(Words, "fr", "{N} members", {N: 0}) --> "0 membre" *)
Words = i18n.Of([i18n.Catalog("fr", [
  (* the line of the connection and the conflicts, Ceres's (web.Connection, web.Conflicts), and the sign-in again:
     first, so that a text filled in is read against these before a template of a wider shape, as {What}: {List} *)
